<beginDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">-477</beginDate>
<endDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">-476</endDate>
<PerseusURI xml:lang="en">Turning a deaf ear to all these proposals, when their ships were manned and their allies had come in, the Corinthians sent a herald before them to declare war, and getting under weigh with seventy-five ships and two thousand heavy infantry, sailed for Epidamnus to give battle to the Corcyraeans.  Thuc. 1.29 Thucydides. The Peloponnesian War. London, J. M. Dent; New York, E. P. Dutton. 1910. http://data.perseus.org/citations/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0003.tlg001.perseus-eng3:1.29</PerseusURI>
<PerseusURI xml:lang="grc">Κορίνθιοι δὲ οὐδὲν τούτων ὑπήκουον, ἀλλ᾽ ἐπειδὴ πλήρεις αὐτοῖς ἦσαν αἱ νῆες καὶ οἱ ξύμμαχοι παρῆσαν, προπέμψαντες κήρυκα πρότερον πόλεμον προεροῦντα Κερκυραίοις, ἄραντες ἑβδομήκοντα ναυσὶ καὶ πέντε δισχιλίοις τε ὁπλίταις ἔπλεον ἐπὶ τὴν Ἐπίδαμνον Κερκυραίοις ἐναντία πολεμήσοντες Thuc. 1.29 Thucydides. Historiae in two volumes. Oxford, Oxford University Press. 1942. http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0003.tlg001.perseus-grc1:1.29</PerseusURI>
</owl:NamedIndividual>
<!--  http://ontologia.fr/OTB/lac#evt-deforestation_Sicily  -->
