<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://ontologia.fr/OTB/lac#Secession">
<PerseusLSJURI xml:lang="el">η απόσυρση μιας ομάδας από μια ευρύτερη οντότητα (ιδίως μια πολιτική οντότητα, αλλά και από οποιαδήποτε οργάνωση, ένωση ή στρατιωτική συμμαχία) που προκαλεί εξέγερση</PerseusLSJURI>
<rdfs:label xml:lang="grc">ἀπόστασις , εως, ἡ, (ἀφίστημι)</rdfs:label>
<PerseusLSJURI xml:lang="en">the withdrawal of a group from a larger entity (especially a political entity, but also from any organization, union or military alliance) causing to revolt</PerseusLSJURI>
<rdfs:label xml:lang="en">secession</rdfs:label>
<PerseusLSJURI xml:lang="grc">https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/morph?l=apostas&la=greek#lexicon</PerseusLSJURI>
<rdfs:label xml:lang="el">αποστασία</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://ontologia.fr/OTB/lac#Sedition">
<rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sedition</rdfs:label>
<rdfs:label xml:lang="el">στάση</rdfs:label>
<skos:altLabel xml:lang="grc">στάσις</skos:altLabel>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://ontologia.fr/OTB/lac#Siege">
<PerseusLSJURI xml:lang="grc">http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus%3Atext%3A1999.04.0057%3Aentry%3Dpoliorki%2Fa</PerseusLSJURI>
<rdfs:label xml:lang="en">siege</rdfs:label>
<rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Siege is an attempt of a belligerent force to break down the resistance of the enemy by preventing egress or ingress of men or entrance of supplies over a considerable period of time.The term is applied chiefly to a military as opposed to a naval attempt and implies investment with troops on all sides of a fortified place (often a city).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label xml:lang="el">πολιορκία</rdfs:label>
<rdfs:seeAlso xml:lang="en">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege</rdfs:seeAlso>
</rdf:Description>
